From: sf2000-linux <sf2000-linux@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] mips: sf2000: disable kernel-side live ROM disk writes

The first userspace kmsg write reaches the live sector mirror hook and then
hangs in the ROM disk_write path on hardware. Keep the retained handoff data
for later experiments, but do not call the ROM writer from Linux while storage
bring-up still needs the LCD console.

---
diff --git a/arch/mips/kernel/setup.c b/arch/mips/kernel/setup.c
index 0cd1e90..15d99ec 100644
--- a/arch/mips/kernel/setup.c
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/setup.c
@@ -418,6 +418,8 @@ static void sf2000_live_write_sector(const char *sector)
 		(sf2000_rom_cache_flush_fn)SF2000_ROM_CACHE_FLUSH_KSEG0;
 	volatile unsigned int *handoff = SF2000_LIVE_HANDOFF_KSEG1;
 
+	return;
+
 	if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MIPS_SF2000))
 		return;
 	if (!sf2000_rom_handoff_present())
